# 🗑️ Smart Sanitation — AI-Assisted Waste Management Platform

> A smarter way to report, prioritize, and manage urban sanitation problems.

Smart Sanitation is a web-based platform designed to improve urban waste management by connecting **citizens, intelligent report analysis, and sanitation authorities** in one system.

Citizens can report sanitation problems such as garbage accumulation, overflowing bins, litter, and other waste-related issues. The system analyzes each report, determines its severity, calculates a priority, and presents the information through an authority dashboard.

The goal is simple:

> **Make sanitation management faster, smarter, and more proactive.**

---

## 🚨 The Problem

Traditional sanitation complaint systems can have several limitations:

- Citizens may not know how to properly report problems.
- Complaints may be treated with the same priority.
- Authorities may struggle to identify urgent sanitation issues.
- Repeated complaints can make sanitation hotspots difficult to identify.
- Citizens often don't know when garbage collection will happen.
- Lack of centralized information can slow down response times.

Smart Sanitation addresses these challenges by combining **citizen reporting, intelligent analysis, priority management, maps, and dashboards**.

---

## 💡 Our Solution

Our platform creates a simple flow:

```text
Citizen
   ↓
Report Sanitation Problem
   ↓
Intelligent Analysis
   ↓
Severity Detection
   ↓
Priority Calculation
   ↓
Database
   ↓
Authority Dashboard
   ↓
Action & Resolution      

⚙️ How It Works
1️⃣ Citizen Reports a Problem

A citizen submits a sanitation complaint through the web application.

The report can contain information such as:

Problem category
Description
Location
Supporting image
2️⃣ Intelligent Report Analysis

The backend analyzes the submitted report using an intelligent classification layer.

The system looks for indicators associated with different levels of sanitation risk and determines:

Problem category
Severity
Confidence
Reasoning

For example, reports containing indicators such as overflowing garbage, sewage, burning waste, dumping, or dead animals can receive higher severity.

3️⃣ Priority Calculation

After analysis, the system calculates a priority for the report.

This helps distinguish between:

Low → Medium → High → Critical

so that urgent sanitation issues can receive faster attention.

4️⃣ Centralized Database

Reports are stored in the backend database so they can be tracked and managed.

This creates a centralized source of sanitation information.

5️⃣ Authority Dashboard

Authorities can access a dashboard containing information about reported problems.

The dashboard provides visibility into:

Total reports
Report status
Priority levels
Sanitation hotspots
Report locations
Garbage collection information
Trucks and routes
6️⃣ Map-Based Monitoring

Sanitation reports can be displayed on an interactive map.

This makes it easier to identify areas where sanitation problems are concentrated.

Over time, this information can help authorities identify sanitation hotspots and recurring problem areas.

7️⃣ Garbage Collection

The platform is designed to support better communication around garbage collection.

Instead of citizens being unsure about when a collection vehicle will arrive, the system can provide collection information and notifications.

🧠 Intelligent Analysis

The current system uses a lightweight rule-based intelligence layer that analyzes report descriptions and identifies sanitation-risk indicators.

Example:

Report:
"Garbage is overflowing onto the road."


        ↓


Keyword / Risk Analysis


        ↓


Severity: HIGH
Confidence: 94%


        ↓


Priority Calculation

The architecture is intentionally designed so that this component can later be replaced or extended with:

Large Language Models
Computer Vision
Image classification
More advanced ML models

without redesigning the entire application.

